":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I'm seeing a very bizarre error when using `expand_location` and `alias` together. Here's a minimalish reproducer:\r\n\r\nhttps://gist.github.com/carl-stripe/b2eef191561b880445c91dafd7f40462\r\n(I just plopped those three files and nothing else into a scratch directory in `/tmp`)\r\n\r\nHere's what happens when I attempt to build:\r\n```\r\n/private/tmp/blub$ bazel build //...\r\nERROR: /private/tmp/blub/BUILD:8:1: in sad rule //:oh_noes:\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n\tFile \"/private/tmp/blub/BUILD\", line 8\r\n\t\tsad(name = 'oh_noes')\r\n\tFile \"/private/tmp/blub/sadness.bzl\", line 2, in _sad_impl\r\n\t\tctx.expand_location(\"$(location :hi)\", ctx.attr.blub)\r\nexpected type 'Target' for 'targets' element but got type 'Target' instead.\r\nERROR: Analysis of target '//:oh_noes' failed; build aborted.\r\n```\r\n\r\nCertainly the error message is a bug—it makes no sense. I suspect the underlying incompatibility is also a bug, but I'm very new to Bazel and could just be misunderstanding something\r\n\r\n### Environment info\r\n`release 0.5.2-homebrew` (also saw it with `0.4.5`) on OS X 10.12.5\r\n\r\n###  Have you found anything relevant by searching the web?\r\nNo (I googled for variants of `expand_location alias`)","closed_by":{"login":"bazel-io","id":15028808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io","html_url":"https://github.com/bazel-io","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/starred{/